"""Lesson 17 student pages, checked source excerpts and UML sequence."""
STYLE+='''select{font:700 21px/1.5 "Segoe UI";padding:16px;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;width:100%}#custom{width:24px;height:24px}#fixture-content{white-space:pre-wrap;font:20px/1.6 Consolas,monospace;color:var(--ink);background:var(--soft);padding:24px;border-radius:16px;max-height:420px;overflow:auto}#notice:empty{display:none}.markdown-body{white-space:normal!important}.markdown-body li{margin:12px 0}#events li{font-size:19px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.json-view{max-height:460px}.workflow-step{scroll-margin-top:20px}'''
(PUBLIC/'style.css').write_text(STYLE,encoding='utf-8')
learn=[('Discover filesystem skills','A skill is a directory containing SKILL.md with a name, description and workflow instructions. The SDK discovers metadata from selected filesystem sources, rather than a programmatic skill-registration API.'),('Load expertise on demand','The model invokes the Skill tool when an available description matches the task. Successful tool evidence and returned skill-specific markers demonstrate observed invocation; the app does not claim to capture every internal prompt block.'),('Choose an invocation scope','Compare omitted skills, "all", an exact-name list and []. When tools is explicit, include Skill. Setting skills auto-adds Skill to allowedTools in the SDK, but explicit tools still governs availability.'),('Read discovery metadata correctly','system/init.skills lists user-invocable skills, including bundled entries, and is not the skills allowlist. A restricted session can still list both classroom skills. user-invocable:false skills are a separate reference case, not created here.'),('Separate direct dispatch from model invocation','Sending /api-review dispatches a user-invocable skill even when it is omitted from the model skills list. Restricting skills is not an OS/file permission boundary. The host separately restricts reads and commands.'),('Troubleshoot with actual evidence','Check cwd and settingSources when skills are missing, description and scope when they are unused, and exact-name syntax when validation fails. The wildcard experiment exercises actual SDK validation before initialization.')]
body='''<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Discover</b><p>Metadata from SKILL.md</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Invoke</b><p>Skill tool or /name dispatch</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Verify</b><p>Init, completed calls and real results</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><h2>How will this session discover and invoke skills?</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta">Checking local server…</p><label for="mode">Skills experiment</label><select id="mode"><option value="all">Enable every discovered skill · "all"</option><option value="omitted">Omit skills · runtime defaults</option><option value="allow-one">Allow only catalog-summary</option><option value="none">Disable model skill invocation · []</option><option value="no-source">Break discovery · settingSources: []</option><option value="slash">/api-review despite a catalog-only model list</option><option value="invalid">Reject wildcard skill name · ["*"]</option></select><p class="note">Two trusted classroom skills live in the owned project. The model can Read only catalog.md, so it cannot fetch SKILL.md to imitate invocation. Summary runs request the matching available workflow; disabled and missing-source runs request a plain summary. Direct dispatch uses an explicit /api-review prompt.</p><button id="run" class="primary" disabled>Run the skills experiment →</button></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><p>Estimated cost: <strong id="cost">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Session: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p class="meta">Omission is genuinely absent from the options object. [] and "all" remain explicit choices. The wildcard case passes the actual invalid list to SDK validation; it does not substitute a hand-written validation result.</p></section></div><section class="step" id="discovery-panel"><h2>Discovery is not invocation permission</h2><pre><code id="discovery" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>The full init message is below. This focused view shows the two classroom names and the total number of init entries, including bundled skills. A name listed here is not proof that the model may invoke it under the current skills list.</p></section><section class="step" id="evidence-panel"><h2>Completed calls and actual response evidence</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="evidence" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>PostToolUse records completed Read and Skill calls. Markers come from the real result, not expected-answer insertion. A directly dispatched /name can load instructions without a model Skill tool call. The host’s file guard is separate from the SDK model-skill allowlist.</p></section><section class="step" id="fixtures-panel"><h2>Inspect the saved classroom skills</h2><label for="fixture">Skill file location</label><select id="fixture"></select><div id="fixture-content" role="region" aria-label="SKILL.md contents">Run an experiment to inspect safe skill fixtures.</div><p>The viewer is a host-rendered student aid, not prompt injection. Skills contain harmless read-only workflows; the SDK loads the selected content internally on invocation.</p></section><section class="step" id="init-panel"><h2>Actual system/init message</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="init" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="run-history"><h2>Compare this browser’s experiments</h2><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Discovered classroom names</th><th>Actual markers</th><th>Completed Skill calls</th><th>Direct dispatch</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div><button id="download">Download actual observations</button></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Actual SDK messages and tools</h2><ul id="events"></ul></section>'''
document('/','Skills that load <em>when invoked.</em>','Explore filesystem discovery, model invocation, exact-name scope and direct command dispatch.',body,'<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
document('/learn.html','What you <em>will learn.</em>','Distinguish available descriptions, allowed invocation and actual completed skill calls.',cards(learn)+actions(('/run.html','Configure and run →'),('/architecture.html','Explore the UML →')))
env=(APP/'.env.example').read_text(encoding='utf-8').strip()
runsteps=[('Prepare the TypeScript application','Use Node.js 24+, npm, your own Anthropic key and model access. Windows may also require Git Bash.','cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson17-skills'),('Install and configure your key','Preserve an existing .env or copy the safe example. Add your own key locally, not in the browser or shared source.','npm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) {\n  Copy-Item .env.example .env\n}\nnotepad .env'),('Start and observe real invocation','Keep the terminal running and open port 3117. Run All, then Omitted. Inspect discovered names, successful Skill calls and the catalogue marker in the actual answer.','npm start\n# http://127.0.0.1:3117'),('Compare an exact list and an empty list','Run Allow one, then None. The init list can still contain both classroom names in the restricted session. The plain-summary case does not invoke a skill.','npm run sample:env -- allow-one\nnpm run sample:env -- none'),('Break discovery and compare direct dispatch','Run No sources and confirm the classroom skills are absent. Then dispatch /api-review with a catalog-only model list and compare the actual response with Skill tool evidence.','npm run sample:env -- no-source\nnpm run sample:env -- slash'),('Exercise real SDK name validation','Run Invalid wildcard. Expect an SDK validation rejection before system/init, not a fabricated model reply. Then inspect the two safe SKILL.md files and the code walkthrough.','npm run sample:env -- invalid\nnpm test')]
body=''
for i,(title,explanation,code) in enumerate(runsteps,1):body+=f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{explanation}</p>'+snippet(code,'powershell')+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Your .env configuration</h2>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>The npm scripts load the optional .env explicitly. Existing shell variables take precedence. Restart after edits. No Managed Agents agent or environment ID is needed.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>If this app is already listening, startup prints its URL. If another service occupies the port, change PORT or stop that service. On Windows set CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH to the installed bash.exe if necessary. Keep optional npm dependencies enabled. Check key/model access if a real query fails; errors are never replaced by a saved answer.</p></section>'
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the app.</em>','Install, set your key, then compare fresh real SDK sessions.',body)
specs=[('Validate the classroom experiment', 'src/agent.ts', 'c=validateConfig(c);', 'Accept only fixed classroom modes. No arbitrary skill code, prompt, path or command can be submitted by the browser.', 0, 1), ('Write real SKILL.md artifacts', 'src/agent.ts', 'for(const file of files)await writeFile', 'The host writes two trusted skills as filesystem artifacts before starting the SDK. Full contents are not inserted into the task prompt.', 1, 4), ('Choose omitted, all, a list or none', 'src/agent.ts', 'if(mode==="omitted")return undefined;', 'The factory preserves actual omission, enables all skills, selects one exact name, disables model invocation, or passes an invalid wildcard for the SDK to reject.', 1, 2), ('Control filesystem discovery', 'src/agent.ts', 'settingSources:c.mode==="no-source"', 'Project source loads classroom skill metadata. The broken-source experiment uses [] while the actual files remain on disk.', 1, 2), ('Expose the Skill tool explicitly', 'src/agent.ts', 'tools:["Read","Skill"],allowedTools:', 'When tools is explicit, Skill must be included. Invocation scope and general tool availability are separate configuration layers.', 1, 2), ('Guard model tool access', 'src/agent.ts', 'if(name==="Skill")return', 'The host supports only the two classroom Skill names and exact catalog.md reads. Read cannot fetch SKILL.md; Bash, Write and Edit are unavailable.', 2, 1), ('Choose model workflow or slash dispatch', 'src/agent.ts', 'const prompt=c.mode==="slash"', 'A normal prompt asks the model to invoke a matching available skill. The slash case deliberately uses /api-review, whose dispatch is independent of the model skills list.', 1, 2), ('Start the actual SDK query', 'src/agent.ts', 'const run=query({prompt,options});', 'The SDK discovers metadata, handles selected skill invocation and owns the model/tool loop. The wildcard mode exercises its real startup validator.', 1, 2), ('Preserve discovery metadata from init', 'src/agent.ts', 'started=true;initSkills=message.skills;', 'The init array lists user-invocable skills and can include bundled entries. It is not the model allowlist, and does not prove invocation.', 2, 1), ('Record completed Skill invocations', 'src/agent.ts', 'if(input.tool_name==="Skill")skillCalls.push', 'A completed Skill tool call is independent evidence of model invocation. Slash dispatch can load a skill without such a tool call.', 2, 1), ('Keep SDK validation errors factual', 'src/agent.ts', 'if(c.mode!=="invalid" || started', 'Only an actual SDK skill-name validation error before init becomes the rejected outcome. Other errors remain failures rather than being relabelled as a successful exercise.', 2, 1), ('Verify files and actual result markers', 'src/agent.ts', 'const savedFilesUnchanged=', 'Compare saved skill hashes and extract markers from actual text. Marker compliance is an observation, not a complete internal prompt audit.', 1, 4), ('Render the readable answer', 'src/client.ts', 'if (e.type === "answer") renderMarkdown', 'Render real assistant Markdown through parsing and sanitization. Keep discovery, completed tools, scope and direct dispatch distinct in the page.', 1, 0)]
steps=[];arrows=[];lanes=['Student UI','Node host','SDK + Claude','Read guard','Private files']
for n,(title,source,anchor,explanation,a,b) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');lines=text.splitlines();idx=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if anchor in l)
 count={3:5,6:3,11:3}.get(n,1);code='\n'.join(lines[idx:idx+count]).strip()
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language='typescript',explanation=explanation,firstLine=idx+1,lastLine=idx+count,anchors=[lines[idx].strip()],sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {n}. {explanation} This source excerpt shows the corresponding application statement.'))
 arrows.append([a,b,f'{n}. {title}'])
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
xs=[170,520,870,1220,1570];svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1740" height="1600" viewBox="0 0 1740 1600"><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#087fff"/></marker></defs><rect width="1740" height="1600" fill="#f4f9ff"/><text x="40" y="52" font-family="Arial" font-size="34" fill="#101a44">Lesson 17 · Discover skills → invoke on demand → verify actual evidence</text>']
for x,label,colour in zip(xs,lanes,['#087fff','#8838ff','#00a977','#8838ff','#ee5425']):svg.append(f'<rect x="{x-150}" y="90" width="300" height="80" rx="16" fill="{colour}"/><text x="{x}" y="139" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-size="27" fill="white">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x} 170 V1550" stroke="#aec6df" stroke-dasharray="8 7"/>')
for i,(a,b,label) in enumerate(arrows):
 x1,x2=xs[a],xs[b];y=245+i*98;svg.append(f'<text x="{min(x1,x2)+10}" y="{y-18}" fill="#142d53" font-family="Arial" font-size="24">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x1} {y} H{x2}" stroke="#087fff" stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>')
(PUBLIC/'architecture.svg').write_text(''.join(svg)+'</svg>',encoding='utf-8')
walk=''
for s in steps:walk+=f'<section class="step workflow-step" id="workflow-step-{s["number"]:02}"><span class="number">{s["number"]:02}</span><h3>{s["number"]}. {s["title"]}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">Source: {s["source"]} · lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]} · selected source; surrounding code omitted</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+'</section>'
document('/architecture.html','Architecture and <em>UML workflow.</em>','Every workflow step includes its corresponding coloured code excerpt.','<a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen prompt selection and query workflow steps"></div>'+walk)
reference=[('Progressive loading', 'Descriptions and names are discovered first; skill instructions load on invocation. The successful Skill call and skill marker demonstrate observed behavior here. The app does not log private raw requests to claim a complete token-level account of progressive disclosure.'), ('Discovery is not scope', 'system/init.skills lists user-invocable skills whether or not they are in the model skills list. user-invocable:false skills can load without appearing there; that frontmatter variant is explained, not authored in this lab.'), ('Exact names and plugins', 'Use exact directory names for these project skills. Plugin skills use plugin:skill names. Empty, padded, wildcard and certain punctuation-containing names are invalid. Plugins and additional-directory naming collisions are reference topics, not executed integrations.'), ('Commands are a separate invocation path', 'The model skills list hides unlisted skills from the model and restricts the Skill tool, but does not block dispatching a user-invocable skill through /name. It is not an OS/file-access boundary. This app blocks direct Read access to skill files and has no Bash tool.'), ('Troubleshooting', 'Missing: check cwd, selected sources and directory location. Unused: check scope and a precise description. Invalid name: use exact supported names or all. The no-source case and real wildcard rejection make two of these failure modes observable.'), ('Classroom boundaries', 'Only two harmless read-only skills are supported by the host guard. Private runtime/home/config paths and disabled auto memory make comparisons controlled; they are not production tenant isolation. Skill instructions remain model guidance rather than guaranteed enforcement.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Follow actual application code and distinguish reference topics from live experiments.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 17 · Skills in the SDK\n\nBased on Lesson17_Skills_in_the_SDK.pptx. Five linked web pages, large text, formatted answers and 13 source-linked UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson17-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson17-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations, use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson17-skills` instead of cloning. Open http://127.0.0.1:3117 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+ and model access are required.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file or copy .env.example. Enter your key locally; do not commit it. Restart after edits. Shell values take precedence over the optional file loaded by npm start.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nOn Windows, set the Git Bash path if needed. Keep optional npm dependencies enabled. A second start recognizes this app; change PORT if another service occupies it.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'+''.join(f'{i}. {a}: {b}\n' for i,(a,b,c) in enumerate(runsteps[3:],1))+'\n```powershell\nnpm run sample:env -- all\nnpm run sample:env -- omitted\nnpm run sample:env -- allow-one\nnpm run sample:env -- slash\nnpm test\n```\n\n`sample` uses only the launching shell environment; `sample:env` loads the optional file. All queries are real and read-only. Prompt and context are fixed classroom choices, not arbitrary browser-supplied source paths.\n\n## How the app was built\n\n'
for s in steps:readme+=f'### {s["number"]}. {s["title"]}\n\n{s["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{s["source"]}`, lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]}. Selected excerpt.\n\n```typescript\n{s["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\nThe app never exposes the expanded internal prompt or inherited environment. Marker flags describe actual text, not complete instruction audits. Runtime skill files and private session context remain local. Private classroom directories are not an OS sandbox. Media, .env, dependencies and runtime files are excluded from Git.\n\n## References\n\n- [Skills in the SDK](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/skills)\n- [Official skill configuration guide](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/skills)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 17 pages and 13 checked UML source snippets.')
